text I look up. The asparagus bacon wrap still in my mouth.
sound A1M.aac
text @[Kyou]
text So what's it like, going out with Ryou?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...?
text I swallow the object in my mouth, and look at Kyou with my head lurched over.
text @[Tomoya]
text What do you mean?
sound A1N.aac
text @[Kyou]
text Are you enjoying it?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I'm having a bit of a problem with coming up with a response.
text Am I enjoying being together with Fujibayashi...
text It's true that Fujibayashi's been with me for the past week.
text However, even so, there hasn't really been anything special.
text It's not like we've made any progress as lovers.
text However, just by having her there, I've come to learn quite a bit about Fujibayashi.
text These are things that I probably would not have learned if we stayed as just classmates.
text At the very least, I think these are things that I discovered because Fujibayashi found the courage to reach out to me.
sound A1O.aac
text @[Kyou]
text ...Do you find it boring...?
text As I stayed in silence, Kyou asks uneasily.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Nah, I think if I had to say one way or another... I'm enjoying it.
text @[Tomoya]
text If I didn't start going out with her, we wouldn't have moments like this.
text @[Tomoya]
text She's really shy, but I really enjoy watching her to try her best to stay by my side.
text @[Tomoya]
text She gets stubborn once fortune telling is brought up, and she gets embarrassed over the tiniest trifles...
text @[Tomoya]
text She's actually bad at cooking and she's much faster than she looks.
text @[Tomoya]
text I probably would never have learned about any of this if we just stayed as friends.
text @[Tomoya]
text It's just as you said. These are things that you can only learn because we are going out.
text @[Tomoya]
text At the very least, I think the past week has been very meaningful.
text Kyou listens to me in silence.
text She then looks at the lunch box and starts thinking.
text I have no idea what was going on in her mind...
